{"path":"numeric/complex/Imaginary_I","title":"_Imaginary_I","titleHtml":"_Imaginary_I","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/complex/Imaginary_I","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"The _Imaginary_I macro expands to a value of type const float _Imaginary with the value of the imaginary unit.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex\"><code>&lt;complex.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"co2\">#define _Imaginary_I /* unspecified */</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The <code>_Imaginary_I</code> macro expands to a value of type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">float</span> _Imaginary</span></code> with the value of the imaginary unit.\n</p><p>As with any pure imaginary number support in C, this macro is only defined if the imaginary numbers are supported.\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-c99 t-until-c11\"><td>\n<p>A compiler that defines <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">__STDC_IEC_559_COMPLEX__</span></code> is not required to support imaginary numbers. POSIX recommends checking if the macro <code>_Imaginary_I</code> is defined to identify imaginary number support.\n</p>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span><br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-c11\">(until C11)</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-c11\"><td>\n<p>Imaginary numbers are supported if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">__STDC_IEC_559_COMPLEX__</span></code> is defined.\n</p>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c11\">(since C11)</span></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This macro allows for the precise way to assemble a complex number from its real and imaginary components, e.g. with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>x <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> _Imaginary_I <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>y<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>. This pattern was standardized in C11 as the macro <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/CMPLX\"><span class=\"kw747\">CMPLX</span></a></span></code>. Note that if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/Complex_I\"><span class=\"kw744\">_Complex_I</span></a></span></code> is used instead, this expression is allowed to convert negative zero to positive zero in the imaginary position.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z1 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> INFINITY <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> _Imaginary_I<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"z1 =&nbsp;%.1f%+.1fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw753\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z1<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw750\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z1<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> INFINITY <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/Complex_I\"><span class=\"kw744\">_Complex_I</span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"z2 =&nbsp;%.1f%+.1fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw753\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw750\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>z1 = 0.0+Infi \nz2 = NaN+Infi</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.1/5 _Imaginary_I (p: 188)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.6/1 _Imaginary_I (p: 537)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.1/3 _Imaginary_I (p: 170)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.6/1 _Imaginary_I (p: 472)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/Complex_I\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>_Complex_I</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   the complex unit constant i <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(macro constant)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/I\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>I</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   the complex or imaginary unit constant i <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(macro constant)</span> </td></tr>\n</table></div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"Complex number arithmetic"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"_Imaginary_I","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. The _Imaginary_I macro expands to a value of type const float _Imaginary with the value of the imaginary unit."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This macro allows for the precise way to assemble a complex number from its real and imaginary components, e.g. with (double complex)((double)x + _Imaginary_I…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"_Complex_I","note":"the complex unit constant i"},{"label":"I","note":"the complex or imaginary unit constant i"}]}]},"standards":["C99","C11"],"wordCount":239,"codeBlockCount":2}
